            "title": "Marble Care and Maintenance",
            "content": "<ul><li>Our Marble products are honed to give a smooth matte texture that is velvety to touch. Caring for your honed marble products to keep them looking pristine requires the following recommendations:</li><li>Wipe spills promptly to avoid them soaking into the surface.  Use a soft microfibre cloth or paper towel to blot, not wipe, so you don't spread the liquid.</li><li>For everyday cleaning, use warm water and mild pH neutral dish soap. Gently wipe down the surface with a dampened soft cloth or microfiber towel.</li><li>Rinse with water after cleaning and dry with a soft cloth.</li><li>Lightly buff the surface with a soft microfibre cloth to help restore the honed finish and remove light stains.</li><li>This can also help maintain the matte appearance of the marble.</li><li>Avoid cleaning products with bleach, ammonia, or acidic ingredients. These can dull the finish or damage the stone over time.</li><li>Avoid direct contact with acidic or oily substances, like coffee, wine, vinegars, cheese, cooking oils, as they can discolour the surface.</li><li>Do not leave marble surfaces wet for long periods. Always dry the marble after cleaning or after exposure to water to avoid water spots and potential stains.</li><li>By following these simple maintenance tips, you'll help preserve your honed marble and keep it looking beautiful without the risk of stains or surface damage.</li></ul>",
